      - the glossary defined an invariant by leading with a ranking magnitude that is not implemented
    readability:
      - the harness section named AgentHarness, ACP and two spec ids before any of them were introduced. It now states the governing role first and names the mechanism second
      - hard gates and weighted objectives appeared six lines in, defined two hundred lines later; the opening now forward-links instead
      - MCP was never expanded anywhere in the README or glossary
      - no cuts were made: the earlier over-cut is recorded, and the audit found the density problem is undefined jargon rather than length

chg_014_spec_review:
  - actor: neuralwatt/glm-5.2-flex via opencode, fresh session per the reviewer-independence rule
    result: REQUEST CHANGES on the first draft; five blockers, all verified against the code and all accepted
    addressed:
      - the draft claimed to close RISK-002. The wired path proposes and validates a Mutation and calls the two-argument score through PhenotypeBridgeScorer; MutationContractValidator.validate is reached only from ConceptualCrossoverPolicy. Both named mechanisms would exist at component level while neither reached the path RISK-002 describes. Title and intent are corrected rather than the scope widened, and S9 now asserts the remaining gap instead of leaving it assumed
      - task T5 was unexecutable: it said to thread the accepted contract from MutationEvaluationLoop, which holds no MutationContract to thread. Replaced with tasks that match what the loop actually has
      - retiring everyOperatorSharesTheObjectiveSetTheScorerAssumes would have removed real protection, because PhenotypeFitnessScorer reads DEFAULT_OBJECTIVES at :73 and :84 precisely on the wired path. The test is kept and its retirement is now a recorded non-goal
      - scenario S5 was unreachable: requireDeterministicObjectives rejects any contract whose objectives differ from operator defaults and every operator shares DEFAULT_OBJECTIVES, so an accepted contract can never declare a different set. The spec now states this and records relaxing the validator as a separate decision
      - the requirement said the scorer decides "never against a fixed assumption", which reads as licence to drop the structural gates. Reworded, and S6 now pins that declared-evidence gates are additional to them
      - added S3 for duplicate results on one declared id with fail-wins, made the substitution rule explicit in S1, and added S7 so declared-evidence gates are emitted under the CON-002 canonical scheme as integrity outcomes rather than introducing a second naming scheme
      - the delta targeted a capability that does not exist; it is now MODIFIED against mutation-fitness-loop, which is CAP-001's name and the scope RISK-002 sits inside
    note: reviewing the spec before implementing cost one model call and prevented writing code against a specification with an unexecutable task and an unreachable scenario

