  - actor: neuralwatt/kimi-k3 via opencode, session ses_fd7d60d1bffeliUItc3o9GR5Em
    result: APPROVE WITH FIXES; all findings addressed
    addressed:
      - the four acceptance scenarios resolved to one check_model_routing_policy call emitting a single combined error, so no scenario had a check that could fail on its own. Each scenario now has section-scoped phrase assertions, verified by three mutations: deleting a substantive control while keeping every heading and identifier, removing the reviewer-independence rule, and moving Q-010 out of its owning section. Each mutation failed exactly one named check
      - `layer: contract` was undocumented and unvalidated. The documented set in .agents/schemas/change.schema.md now lists every in-use value, and check-changes enforces it so the schema and the specs cannot drift apart again
