completed:
  - created CHG-012 to codify bounded provider-session reuse, source-referenced context packets, explicit role-based multi-model usage, budget telemetry, reset/escalation rules and reviewer independence without automatic routing
  - strengthened AGENTS and `.agents/coordination/MODEL_ROUTING_POLICY.md`; a repository-contract check now requires its session, context/budget, multi-model and audit/safety controls plus Q-010/Q-011/ARCH-001/RISK-001 links
  - added PAT-002, updated the profile and architecture/development/wiki guidance, and documented that unavailable provider usage/cost telemetry must not be invented
  - completed CHG-011 tasks T1-T5; full validation and two-pass lead review are ready for independent review
  - created CHG-011 with scenario-to-test mappings for a deterministic session lifecycle, catalog/route/target inspection, and governed workflow/code evolution
  - added provider-free `HarnessSessionStateMachine` plus session state/target domain vocabulary; closed sessions reject later mutations
  - added `saaa sa`, a line-oriented interactive control-plane client with capability/skill/profile inspection, explicit `HARNESS_WORKFLOW` or `CODE` target selection, explicit route selection, and `evolve` dispatch through the existing EvolveRunner
  - proved fixture-backed workflow and Java code targets both use the existing isolated candidate/check/fitness/decision path; code realization remains whole-file and not AST-aware
  - updated README, architecture/operations wiki and PROJECT_PROFILE to record `saaa sa`, its MCP boundary, and the deliberate interactive-command namespace exception
  - reconciled stale follow-ups: removed the already-merged CHG-008 PR/validation action, removed the absent `feat/first-vertical-slice` cleanup, and collapsed duplicate CHG-002 T4b entries
  - added CHG-009 with ACP-over-stdio scenarios, acceptance mappings and opt-in real-agent follow-up
  - pinned the official ACP Java SDK 0.14.0 in the adapters module
  - implemented AcpAgentHarness and AcpAgentConfig with initialize/session/prompt lifecycle, streamed text digest, bounded mutation parsing, timeout/failure mapping and exhausted-budget rejection
  - added ACP adapter tests for mutation parsing, malformed output, failed subprocess evidence and budget rejection
  - updated README, architecture wiki and PROJECT_PROFILE to record ACP as the first real external adapter
  - lead review bounded ACP streamed output to 65536 characters and redacted common bearer/API-key patterns in failure evidence
  - added CHG-006 with scenarios, acceptance mappings, completed tasks and explicit follow-up for ACP and concrete external harness adapters
  - added provider-neutral AgentRequest, AgentRoute, ResourceBudget, AgentUsage, AgentRunResult and AgentRunStatus domain records
