fitness_functions:
  - added: evolve pre-flight now rejects a workflow target that equals a declared behaviour-case grader, preventing candidates from rewriting their own check script; acceptance coverage proves rejection occurs before journaling or candidate creation
  - changed: fitness identifiers now use `subject.invariant.*`, `subject.objective.*` and `process.invariant.*` forms through `FitnessSignalId`; weights, threshold, derivations and decisions are unchanged; MCP grouping uses typed force and legacy keys are normalized at the output boundary
  - changed: PR `pull_request` CI runs the fast conformance profile (`project check`, `project check-readme`, `project test`, `project component-test`, `project integration-test`, `project lint`) and no longer runs `project ready`; automatic `push` to `main`, `v*` tags and manual `profile=full` dispatch run both fast checks and full readiness
  - removed: the separate `repo-contract` workflow is deleted because `project check` runs `check-repo-contract` in the main CI workflow
  - unchanged: T1 adds LangChain4j OpenAI provider wiring only inside `modules/adapters/src/main/java/com/dreamthought/saaa/adapters/langchain4j`; the boundary fitness function remains the guard that provider imports do not leak into `modules/domain` or `modules/deterministic`
  - added: `hard_gate_non_empty_realization` in `PhenotypeFitnessScorer` fails promotion closed when the realization changed no file; enforced by test rather than by the boundary script, like the `CommandCheckRunner` containment rule
  - unchanged: `check-architecture-boundaries` still fails loudly when a scanned layer directory is missing, and `modules/domain` and `modules/deterministic` still import only `java.*` and repository packages
  - added: `DiffLineBudgetMutationValidator` rejects proposal diffs over `maxLinesChanged` before candidate worktree creation; covered by CLI ATDD and deterministic unit tests
  - unchanged: no layer boundary moved; provider capture stays in `modules/adapters/langchain4j`, candidate TOON writing stays in `modules/adapters/git`, and deterministic/domain code sees only provider-neutral records and ports
  - added: behaviour-case child processes run with an explicit allow-listed environment; covered by adapter integration and CLI acceptance tests
  - added: promotion is branch-pointer-only at the `CandidateDecisionSink` port via `CandidateBranchRef`, with unit coverage for the type shape and a deterministic source scan for merge commands
  - added: `check-architecture-boundaries` rejects candidate auto-merge command references in deterministic, adapter and CLI main sources, so the invariant runs in PR CI
  - unchanged by the README evidence pass: no gate, weight, threshold or scoring path was modified. The pass documented the existing fitness function precisely and recorded its weaknesses as risks and next actions rather than changing behaviour
  - added: `check-glossary` fails `project check` when a load-bearing glossary term or the `CON-002` reference goes missing; it verifies presence and the pointer, not ordering and not that the pointer resolves

