  no_record: |
    CHG-012 adds PAT-002 because the session/budget/multi-model practice is durable and cross-task. It does not add a new routing decision because automatic runtime routing remains explicitly deferred by Q-010 and Q-011.

    `T2/T2b` implement tasks already recorded in `CHG-004`; the durable record is the task status,
    the new adapter tests and this handoff rather than a new knowledge entry.

    The README evidence pass created no new knowledge entry. It is documentation-only and changed
    no behaviour or boundary, so there is no spec delta to record. The three implementation
    concerns it surfaced (check-script-as-mutation-target, the inert weighted objectives, the
    `reliability` substring test) are recorded under `risks` and `next` above. Promote them to
    `RISK-` entries when someone picks up the fix, because that is the point at which they acquire
    an owner and a revisit condition.

    Fitness taxonomy step 1 shipped without a `CHG-` spec. It changes no behaviour, no
    boundary and no acceptance scenario: it adds a documentation check, glossary entries and
    one knowledge entry recording a target shape that is explicitly not in force. The durable
    record is `CON-002`, this handoff and the design note. Steps 2 onward do change behaviour
    and each needs its own spec.

team_fallback:
  current: single_lead_with_pr_review_gate
  fitness_signal_id_review: attempted a low-cost local opencode review worker, but the installed CLI could not start model discovery because it could not open its configured log path; no independent worker findings were obtained. Compensating evidence is focused legacy-key regression coverage, full unit/component/integration/readiness validation, lead diff review and the required human PR review gate.
  reason: the active collaboration contract prohibited spawning subagents for CHG-005, so the lead performed explicit architecture/security/efficiency self-review and preserved human review as the required PR merge gate; no merge or push was attempted
  chg_005_lost_challenge: no independent actor reviewed this large slice before handoff; compensating evidence is outside-in acceptance coverage, real Git/SQLite/Neo4j integration, Nix operator exercises, dependency/image scanning and an explicit 14-question lead challenge
  chg_005_outcome: PR #18 merged 2026-08-04 as `4cac837` after human review; the merge gate was human review plus clean-checkout CI. Clean-checkout CI, not review, is what caught the test-isolation defect, which is evidence that the missing independent-actor challenge was a real gap rather than a formality
  chg_003_outcome: PR #1 "Run one mutation evaluation end to end (CHG-003)" merged 2026-07-30; two independent actor reviews during its development, the second of which found a surviving promotion-integrity hole and returned do-not-merge before the `T11` fix
  t10_outcome: PR #2 "Hard-gate a candidate whose realization changed nothing (CHG-003 T10)" merged 2026-07-31 as `3f64b8a` after human review; the code change had lead self-review only, no independent actor review, but was covered test-first and the failing acceptance test was observed reporting PROMOTE before the gate existed
  readme_rework_outcome: pushed directly to `main` as `afcf76a` under explicit user authorization, no PR; lead self-review only, no actor or human review pass, no code changes
  lost_challenge: the T10 code change and the README rework did not receive independent actor review; the T10 change has automated acceptance and unit coverage, the README change is a docs-only edit

task_path:
  chunks:
    - id: C7
      work: rewrite main's history to strip Claude session URLs from commit messages
      depends_on: every open branch and worktree landed on main first, so nothing has to be rebased across the rewrite
      authorised_by: owner, 2026-08-22, who also assessed the exposure as low because the links are auth-gated
      scope: 79 commits on main across six distinct sessions, 2026-07-28 to 2026-08-22
      before_starting:
        - land C1 through C6 and remove every worktree except the coordination checkout, because every surviving branch would need rebasing onto rewritten history
        - AGENTS.md forbids force-pushing main without explicit authorisation; cite the authorisation recorded here
        - expect every SHA on main to change. HANDOFF.toon, the specs, PAT and LRN entries and merged PR bodies all cite SHAs that will stop resolving; decide whether to rewrite those references or accept them as historical
      status: committed. The owner reaffirmed on 2026-08-22 that the historic commit messages are to be fixed once every worktree is merged. This is not optional tidying and must not be dropped from a later handoff
      method:
        - confirm no branch or worktree other than the coordination checkout survives, and that origin has no open PR
        - FILTER_BRANCH_SQUELCH_WARNING=1 git filter-branch -f --msg-filter "sed '/^Claude-Session:/d'" -- --all
        - verify with: git log --all --format=%B | grep -c Claude-Session, which must print 0
        - verify the tree is unchanged: the rewrite touches messages only, so every resulting tree hash must match its original
        - push with --force-with-lease, which needs the owner authorisation recorded above because AGENTS.md otherwise forbids force-pushing main
        - re-clone or reset any other checkout afterwards; existing clones keep the old history
      sha_references: HANDOFF.toon, the specs, PAT and LRN entries and merged PR bodies cite SHAs that stop resolving after the rewrite. Fix the in-repo references in the same change; merged PR bodies on the host cannot be fixed and stay as historical record
      honest_limit: rewriting does not remove the data already published. The original commits stay fetchable by SHA on the host, remain visible in pull request views, and exist in every clone and fork already taken. The rewrite cleans the tip, not the record. It is still worth doing so the canonical history is clean, and the owner has accepted that limit
      prevention_already_landed: CHG-015 forbids credential-shaped strings in commit messages and guards it, so the count cannot grow while C7 waits

